    "tag": "SOURCED",
    "citation": "U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics, Current Population Survey, Table 53 'Certification and licensing status of the employed by occupation', 2023 annual averages, https://www.bls.gov/cps/data/aa2023/cpsaat53.pdf. A license is awarded by a government agency and conveys a legal authority to work in an occupation; a certification is issued by a non-governmental body. All employed: 21.6 percent hold a license, 2.5 percent a certification only (Table 49, https://www.bls.gov/cps/data/aa2023/cpsaat49.pdf)."
